ef 17592186045485 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420259 1071 "Let $x,y,$ and $z$ be integers. If $z∣xy$ and $\\text{gcd}(z,x)=1$ then\n\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420259 1072 #uuid "360410c4-4e76-5ee1-ae9a-a22c317dc4de" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420259 1074 "For any integers $x,$ $y,$ and $z,$ we have that\n\n$$\nz∣xy\\,\\text{and}\\,\\text{gcd}(z,x)=1\\,⟹\\,z∣y.\n$$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420260 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420254 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420260 1069 "q-93649" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420260 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420260 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $10\\,|\\,21b$ then $10\\,|\\,b$\n- If $21\\,|\\,25b$ then $21\\,|\\,b$\n- If $15\\,|\\,9b$ then $15\\,|\\,b$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420260 1072 #uuid "42a248b1-4b2a-5a7f-b673-589ac28da9a8" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420260 1074 "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1.$ Therefore, we have $10\\,|\\,21b$ and $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1,$ which implies $10\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(21,25)=1.$ Therefore, we have $21\\,|\\,25b$ and $\\text{gcd}(21,25)=1,$ which implies $21\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $b=5.$ Then, $15∣9\\cdot 5$ but $15∤5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420261 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420245 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420261 1069 "q-93650" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420261 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420261 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,19b$ then ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If $12\\,|\\,35b$ then $12\\,|\\,b$\n- If $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ then $22\\,|\\,b$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420261 1072 #uuid "553ed68f-8e74-5dda-a8b3-cdd3e89c31cb" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420261 1074 "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let $b=19.$ Then, ${19}^{2}∣19\\cdot 19$ but ${19}^{2}∤19.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1.$ Therefore, we have $12\\,|\\,35b$ and $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1,$ which implies $12\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1.$ Therefore, we have $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ and $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1,$ which implies $22\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420262 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420255 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420262 1069 "q-93657" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420262 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420262 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $3\\,|\\,a$ and $2\\,|\\,a$ then $6\\,|\\,a$\n- If $7\\,|\\,b$ and $14\\,|\\,b$ then $98\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${2}^{3}\\,|\\,c$ and $3\\,|\\,c$ then $24\\,|\\,c$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420262 1072 #uuid "5ddd359d-678b-53c8-9991-000fcf922944" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420262 1074 "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a\\,|\\,c,$ $\\,b\\,|\\,c,\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $ab\\,|\\,c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(2,3)=1$ and $2\\cdot 3=6.$ Therefore, we have $(2\\,|\\,a),(3\\,|\\,a),$ and $\\text{gcd}(2,3)=1,$ which implies $(6\\,|\\,a).$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=14.$ Then, $(7∣14)$ and $(14∣14),$ but $(98∤14).$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({2}^{3},3)=1$ and ${2}^{3}\\cdot 3=24.$ Therefore, we have $({2}^{3}\\,|\\,c),(3\\,|\\,c),$ and $\\text{gcd}({2}^{3},3)=1,$ which implies $(24\\,|\\,c).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420263 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420253 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420263 1069 "q-221372" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420263 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420263 1071 "Let $s,t$ and $u$ be integers. If $u∣t$ and $t∣s,$ then\n\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420263 1072 #uuid "6cb148c3-0ff5-5200-b071-d1495f25735d" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420263 1074 "For any integers $s,$ $t,$ and $u,$ we have that\n\n$$\nu∣t\\,\\text{and}\\,t∣s\\,⟹\\,u∣s.\n$$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420264 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420248 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420264 1069 "q-93658" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420264 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420264 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $4\\,|\\,a$ and $9\\,|\\,a$ then $36\\,|\\,a$\n- If $5\\,|\\,b$ and $7\\,|\\,b$ then $35\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${6}^{2}\\,|\\,c$ and $2\\,|\\,c$ then $72\\,|\\,c$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420264 1072 #uuid "6d7153a0-178f-57d1-b332-d3ea8e076028" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420264 1074 "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a\\,|\\,c,$ $\\,b\\,|\\,c,\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $ab\\,|\\,c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(4,9)=1$ and $4\\cdot 9=36.$ Therefore, we have $(4\\,|\\,a),(9\\,|\\,a),$ and $\\text{gcd}(4,9)=1,$ which implies $(36\\,|\\,a).$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(5,7)=1$ and $5\\cdot 7=35.$ Therefore, we have $(5\\,|\\,b),(7\\,|\\,b),$ and $\\text{gcd}(5,7)=1,$ which implies $(35\\,|\\,b).$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $c=36.$ Then, $({6}^{2}∣36)$ and $(2∣36),$ but $(72∤36).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420265 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420244 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420265 1069 "q-221379" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420265 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420265 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $12∣h$ then $4∣h$\n- If $4∣h$ then $2∣h$\n- If $3∣h$ then $12∣h$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420265 1072 #uuid "73c135de-ad71-58aa-a780-c01d04341240" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420265 1074 "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $4∣12.$ Therefore, we have\n$4∣12$ and $12∣h,$ which implies that $4∣h.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $2∣4.$ Therefore, we have\n$2∣4$ and $4∣h,$ which implies that $2∣h.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $h=3.$ Then, $3∣3$ but $12∤3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420266 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420256 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420266 1069 "q-221465" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420266 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420266 1071 "Let $l,m,$ and $n$ be integers. If $m∣l,$ $n∣l,$ and $\\text{gcd}(m,n)=1$ then\n\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420266 1072 #uuid "9f50d1b1-0f30-55bf-aeb5-6bf553fa9e40" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420266 1074 "For any integers $m,$ $n,$ and $l,$ we have that\n\n$$\nm∣l,\\,n∣l,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\text{gcd}(m,n)=1\\,⟹\\,mn∣l.\n$$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420267 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420250 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420267 1069 "q-221373" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420267 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420267 1071 "Let $g,h$ and $k$ be integers. If $g∣h$ and $h∣k,$ then\n\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420267 1072 #uuid "aea6db90-17cf-56a2-9d48-5e13d8af9223" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420267 1074 "For any integers $k,$ $m,$ and $n,$ we have that\n\n$$\ng∣h\\,\\text{and}\\,h∣k\\,⟹\\,g∣k.\n$$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420268 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420247 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420268 1069 "q-221371" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420268 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420268 1071 "Let $p,q$ and $r$ be integers. If $p∣q$ and $q∣r,$ then\n\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420268 1072 #uuid "bb3ce97a-5535-5c1b-80e8-b47b040c493e" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420268 1074 "For any integers $p,$ $q,$ and $r,$ we have that\n\n$$\np∣q\\,\\text{and}\\,q∣r\\,⟹\\,p∣r.\n$$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420269 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420252 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420269 1069 "q-93648" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420269 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420269 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,10b$ then ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${17}^{2}\\,|\\,17b$ then ${17}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If $20\\,|\\,{3}^{3}b$ then $20\\,|\\,b$" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420269 1072 #uuid "f3b9fb7f-2262-5e34-bb97-3a915acfa755" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true] [17592186420269 1074 "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},10)=1.$ Therefore, we have ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,10b$ and $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},10)=1,$ which implies ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=17.$ Then, ${17}^{2}∣17\\cdot 17$ but ${17}^{2}∤17.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(20,{3}^{3})=1.$ Therefore, we have $20\\,|\\,{3}^{3}b$ and $\\text{gcd}(20,{3}^{3})=1,$ which implies $20\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534366 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-04afe3b6-7b92-50ca-9d72-d4d366016b98" 17592186420185 "answer-06c38ff4-4134-5851-a52f-d46fca4ccc12" 17592186420186 "answer-0acc3059-38a5-5c94-8986-a899f4559838" 17592186420187 "answer-0cbae4e4-2423-5869-9afa-da82e1b33b03" 17592186420188 "answer-0de558f3-abda-56d7-ae48-3fbabe1ad77c" 17592186420189 "answer-142f0a78-ef1b-5c40-b87c-2e4e6e998e29" 17592186420190 "answer-144822ca-c64b-5d44-988e-8d3f58310385" 17592186420191 "answer-25938baa-529b-5f86-828c-2801671fe4d3" 17592186420192 "answer-28a1ea30-a1c0-5800-8caf-4ea2604323dc" 17592186420193 "answer-29b4ecfe-b0b5-5ad3-aa03-585d63c93876" 17592186420194 "answer-2c9e8a01-7b72-52e5-88d6-74925443496f" 17592186420195 "answer-2e1582c6-f975-57a2-bb84-29de70274193" 17592186420196 "answer-35de53fc-7740-5f42-aef3-a33cd4fdcce8" 17592186420197 "answer-37d1ed1f-2a27-5962-9f76-7e68504f6b25" 17592186420198 "answer-3b3e53e1-5077-5ac1-8c4a-f09e11758090" 17592186420199 "answer-3cabb55e-40d7-5b81-a1ac-1144923f9b49" 17592186420200 "answer-47123b5a-4d9e-5980-b7e8-1b9b31e1fa9c" 17592186420201 "answer-4ba3500e-7378-5987-8d40-8972a2087e81" 17592186420202 "answer-4c2ecc2e-8bcf-5a0d-ba77-6ec986871206" 17592186420203 "answer-5070c287-d44b-5c20-a230-09d48693212c" 17592186420204 "a